      },
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9773d57_6e0a07a1",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1228,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125174
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-21T18:58:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please explain why this is video ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1228,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 1228,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c168a0c_aa2d1a29",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1228,
      "author": {
        "id": 1236087
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-08T08:08:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per 3GPP TS 29002 MAP Specification : Section 17.7.10, the BearerServiceCode for \"allDataCircuitAsynchronous\" is \u002701010000\u0027 ( i.e. 80). Hence, SERVICE_CLASS_DATA_SYNC (1\u003c\u003c4) and SERVICE_CLASS_PACKET (1\u003c\u003c6) together make video service class.\nAlso, the same is used in GsmMMiCode.java (http://androidxref.com/8.0.0_r4/xref/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/gsm/GsmMmiCode.java#472)",
      "parentUuid": "f9773d57_6e0a07a1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1228,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 1228,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67ce8534_68cf5a8c",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1228,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125174
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-27T19:41:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Add this response as a comment in code.",
      "parentUuid": "0c168a0c_aa2d1a29",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1228,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 1228,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45e28d82_ca874f6c",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1259,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125174
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-21T18:58:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How is that we do not need number for the video option but we need it for voice?",
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f4e525e8_73dab742",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1259,
      "author": {
        "id": 1236087
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-08T08:08:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per 3GPP spec TS31102, the call forwarding indication status needs to be stored in elementary file, EFCFIS. Hence, for voice, we are storing status and number. But, there seems no provision for storing another number in the EF(say for Video). Hence, we are storing only the status for video call forwarding in preferences to show appropriate indicator.",
      "parentUuid": "45e28d82_ca874f6c",
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b6e26a7_1f348d8c",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1259,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125174
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-27T19:41:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason we store in EFCIS is because we can retain CF status easily if user switches the SIM card to a different phone. If we do not store video call forwarding status, how will the user know that his video calls are being forwarded?\n\nCan you describe the behavior user will see after he switch the SIM to a new phone?",
      "parentUuid": "f4e525e8_73dab742",
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7698ad3_dd6b26ed",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1328,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125174
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-21T18:58:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why cant we make this generic for voice and video ?",
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5bef16ea_2c9678ea",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1328,
      "author": {
        "id": 1236087
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-08T08:08:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "setVoiceCallForwardingFlag API is responsible for storing the call forward info in the elementary file. Currently, there is provision to store only voice CF related info in the EF CFIS. Hence, we cannot make it generic.",
      "parentUuid": "b7698ad3_dd6b26ed",
      "revId": "d02e1aeb7d1cb2cf622725b1a0623ab03ee72795",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
